#!/usr/bin/env node
// Ported from joomlart-t4-template@1.0.0-tracy.5 scripts/make-design-spec.mjs — WordPress changes: the identity, token-taxonomy and naming sections speak theme.json / block patterns / template parts instead of T4 profiles, ACM and module chrome; the dark hook defaults to html[data-theme="dark"].
// make-design-spec.mjs — emit the design-spec artifact (Markdown) from a parsed page-map.
//
// The design-spec is the WRITTEN hand-off that execute subagents (chrome / pattern / CSS builders)
// read INSTEAD of conversation context (see references/inputs/spec-pack.md §2 + references/build-subagents.md §C).
// This generator pre-fills everything the Phase-2 page-map already knows (theme identity, palette
// light+dark, fonts, the page/template/layout list) and leaves explicit `TODO` slots for the values
// that only settle at Phase 6 (token names, type scale, spacing) or need a human (per-section source +
// image pointers, class prefix). Dependency-free: reads JSON, writes Markdown.
//
// Usage:
//   node scripts/make-design-spec.mjs <page-map.json | -> [--out <file>]
//   node scripts/parse-html-bundle.mjs <bundle> | node scripts/make-design-spec.mjs -

import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'

const args = process.argv.slice(2)
let src = null,
  out = null
for (let i = 0; i < args.length; i++) {
  if (args[i] === '--out') out = args[++i]
  else if (!src) src = args[i]
}
if (!src) {
  console.error('usage: make-design-spec.mjs <page-map.json | -> [--out <file>]')
  process.exit(2)
}

const raw = src === '-' ? readFileSync(0, 'utf8') : readFileSync(src, 'utf8')
let map
try {
  map = JSON.parse(raw)
} catch (e) {
  console.error('cannot parse page-map JSON:', e.message)
  process.exit(2)
}

const tpl = map.template || {}
const name = tpl.name || '<slug>'
const title = tpl.title || '<Title>'
// Theme naming rule: references/inputs/spec-pack.md §2.
const themeName = title.startsWith('JA ') ? `WP ${title.slice(3)}` : title
const Tpl = (themeName || name).replace(/(^|\s)\S/g, (s) => s.toUpperCase())
const pal = (map.theme && map.theme.palette) || {}
const light = pal.light || {}
const dark = pal.dark || {}
const fonts = (map.theme && map.theme.fonts) || {}
const pages = Array.isArray(map.pages) ? map.pages : []
const parts = Array.isArray(map.templateParts) ? map.templateParts : []

const TODO = '`TODO`'
const v = (x) => (x ? `\`${x}\`` : TODO)

// palette rows: the 4 the parser extracts are auto-filled; the rest are TODO (read at Phase 6).
const palRow = (key, note) => `| \`${key}\` | ${v(light[key])} | ${v(dark[key])} | ${note} |`

const md = `# Design Spec — ${themeName} (\`${name}\`)

> **Generated by \`scripts/make-design-spec.mjs\` from the Phase-2 page-map.** This is the AUTHORITATIVE
> hand-off artifact for the execute subagents (chrome / pattern / CSS builders) — they read THIS, not
> the conversation. Auto-filled fields come from the page-map; **resolve every slot marker before
> dispatching any execute subagent** (the slots are the values that settle at Phase 6 or need a
> human). Contract + how-to: \`references/inputs/spec-pack.md\` §2.

## 1. Identity
- **Theme slug (\`<TPL>\`, directory + text domain):** \`${name}\`
- **Title (style.css \`Theme Name\`; the readme.txt title and the pattern category label carry the same name):** ${themeName}
- **Dark hook (\`<DARK>\`):** ${TODO} — pin in Phase 0 (default \`html[data-theme="dark"]\`; a class hook such as \`html.is-dark\` is a per-project override; see \`css-tokenizing.md\` §3a)
- **Class prefix:** ${TODO} — e.g. \`${name}-\` (used on every authored pattern/part/override; block classes stay \`wp-block-*\`)

## 2. Palette — light AND dark (route ALL color through these)
| token | light | dark | note |
|---|---|---|---|
${palRow('primary', 'dominant accent: CTA/link')}
${palRow('secondary', 'supporting brand')}
${palRow('body_bg', 'page surface')}
${palRow('text', 'default body text')}
| \`border\` | ${TODO} | ${TODO} | faint divider (read at Phase 6) |
| \`heading\` | ${TODO} | ${TODO} | if headings differ from body text |
| \`surface\` | ${TODO} | ${TODO} | band / card background |

> Dark MIRRORS light, every state. Every slot above becomes a \`theme.json\` \`settings.color.palette\`
> entry (\`--wp--preset--color--<slug>\`) and its dark companion is remapped under \`<DARK>\`.

## 3. Type scale
- **Body font:** ${v(fonts.body)} · **Heading font:** ${v(fonts.heading)}
- **h1–h6 size / weight / line-height:** ${TODO} (read off rendered \`<h1>\`…\`<h6>\`, not the stylesheet — Phase 6)
- **Body size / line-height / letter-spacing:** ${TODO}
- ⚠️ **Pin these in \`theme.json\` (\`settings.typography.fontFamilies\`, \`fontSizes\`, \`styles.typography\`,
  \`styles.elements.h1…h6\`), not only in \`style.css\`** — global styles the user saves in the editor
  override stylesheet rules, and a blank theme's defaults silently win otherwise.

## 4. Spacing
- **Section vertical rhythm (full-width group top/bottom padding):** ${TODO}
- **Content width (\`settings.layout.contentSize\`):** ${TODO} · **Wide width (\`wideSize\`):** ${TODO} · **Card internal padding:** ${TODO}

## 5. Token taxonomy (use these names so every agent routes consistently)
- Brand: \`settings.color.palette\` slugs \`primary\`, \`secondary\`, \`body-bg\`, \`text\` → \`--wp--preset--color--*\`.
- Type: \`settings.typography.fontFamilies\` slugs \`body\`, \`heading\` → \`--wp--preset--font-family--*\`; sizes via \`fontSizes\`.
- Spacing: \`settings.spacing.spacingSizes\` → \`--wp--preset--spacing--*\`; layout via \`settings.layout\`.
- Dark companions: the \`<DARK>\` token-remap block in the theme stylesheet (\`style.css\` or \`assets/css/dark.css\`).
- (Add any theme-specific token names you introduce here so builders reuse them verbatim.)

## 6. Per-artifact source pointers (which bundle markup each builder must match, pixel-for-pixel)
Declared template parts: ${parts.length ? parts.map((p) => `\`${p}\``).join(', ') : TODO}

| page (source file) | template | layout | sections / patterns → source + image assets |
|---|---|---|---|
${
  pages.length
    ? pages
        .map((p) => `| \`${p.file || '?'}\` | \`${p.view || '?'}\` | \`${p.layout || '—'}\` | ${TODO} |`)
        .join('\n')
    : `| ${TODO} | | | |`
}

> For each pattern / template / template part a builder will author, fill the last column with the
> exact source section + the image asset (export the DARK mockup; \`media\` field, not hand-drawn SVG).

## 7. Naming conventions
- **Pattern titles:** \`[${Tpl}] <Page> - <Section>\` (findable in the pattern inserter; \`editability-standards.md\` §7).
- **Pattern slugs:** \`${name}/<page>-<section>\` (\`Slug:\` header in \`patterns/*.php\`); categories \`${name}\`.
- **Template parts:** \`parts/<name>.html\` with the same names declared above; areas \`header\` / \`footer\` / \`uncategorized\`.
- **Text domain:** \`${name}\` — every translatable string in a pattern goes through \`esc_html__( '…', '${name}' )\`.
`

if (out) {
  writeFileSync(out, md)
  console.error(`wrote ${out}`)
} else process.stdout.write(md)
